//   2. matches a protocol-ledger prefix (TRADE/USING/FREE/LEASE-BREAK/
//      BASE/CLAIM/HELLO/OFFER) -> Discord/log only, same as case 3 below.
//   3. anything else -> routine narration, routed through announce('status',
//      ...) (Discord status feed when configured, else runner log only —
//      see announce() above).
//
// TOTAL DE-CHAT DECREE (chief, 2026-09-01): game chat = real talk only, full
// stop. Case 2 above used to be REAL WHITE CHAT, sent verbatim, because
// other bots/tribes parsed public chat for these exact prefixes. That is no
// longer true: inter-tribe coordination moved to the claims registry + repo/
// Discord (monkeorg/cavecrew-mcp#1), so nothing outside the crew needs these
// off public chat anymore, and case 2 now collapses into case 3 — same
// announce('status', ...) route DEPOT already got in the earlier DEPOT
// DE-CHAT decree. PROTOCOL_PREFIX itself stays defined and exported-in-spirit
// (still matched below, just no longer branches anywhere different) because
// the runner's INBOUND chat parsing — hearing FEL's own protocol lines off
// real chat — is untouched by this decree: we stop EMITTING these prefixes
// as white chat, we keep LISTENING for them same as always. Drivers keep
// sending every ledger line exactly as before, via /chat, unchanged format —
// only the destination moved, identical to the DEPOT precedent. KNOWN
// CONSEQUENCE (same shape as DEPOT's): any downstream tooling that greps the
// server's real chat log for these prefixes (scoreboard.mjs already had this
// problem for DEPOT) goes silent on protocol lines too until repointed at
// the Discord feed / claims registry.
const PROTOCOL_PREFIX = /^(TRADE |USING |FREE |LEASE-BREAK |BASE |CLAIM |HELLO |OFFER )/;

async function smartChat(text) {
  const msg = String(text);
  if (msg.startsWith('!')) {
    const stripped = msg.slice(1).trim();
    try {
      bot?.chat?.(stripped);
    } catch {
      // ignore — no bot to talk through either, nothing more to do
    }
    return;
  }
  // TOTAL DE-CHAT DECREE — protocol-ledger lines route exactly like DEPOT:
  // announce('status', ...) (Discord status feed / log), never bot.chat.
  // PROTOCOL_PREFIX.test() is still evaluated (kept for any code that wants
  // to distinguish a protocol line from routine narration downstream — see
  // decree comment above) but no longer changes where the message goes.
  void PROTOCOL_PREFIX.test(msg);
  await announce('status', msg);
}

